From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 12:48:49 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-csi: Only stop the source if it was started

A pattern supplying the input means the source is never started, but it
was still being stopped, and the v4l2 core tracks each sub-device's
streaming state and warns on a stop that follows no start:

  WARNING: drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-subdev.c:484 at call_s_stream
    call_s_stream from sun6i_csi_bridge_s_stream
    sun6i_csi_bridge_s_stream from call_s_stream
    call_s_stream from sun6i_csi_capture_stop_streaming

That fired on every capture taken from a pattern.

Remember whether the source was started rather than asking again on the
way down. The knob that decides it lives in debugfs and can move while a
stream is running, so the question does not necessarily have the same
answer at both ends.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.c |  8 +++++++-
 drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.h | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.c b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.c
@@ -481,7 +481,11 @@ static int sun6i_csi_bridge_s_stream(struct v4l2_subdev *subdev, int on)
 	}
 
 	if (!on) {
-		v4l2_subdev_call(source_subdev, video, s_stream, 0);
+		if (bridge->source_streaming) {
+			v4l2_subdev_call(source_subdev, video, s_stream, 0);
+			bridge->source_streaming = false;
+		}
+
 		ret = 0;
 		goto disable;
 	}
@@ -526,6 +530,8 @@ static int sun6i_csi_bridge_s_stream(struct v4l2_subdev *subdev, int on)
 		ret = v4l2_subdev_call(source_subdev, video, s_stream, 1);
 		if (ret && ret != -ENOIOCTLCMD)
 			goto disable;
+
+		bridge->source_streaming = true;
 	}
 
 	return 0;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.h b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.h
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.h
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.h
@@ -49,6 +49,16 @@ struct sun6i_csi_bridge {
 
 	struct sun6i_csi_bridge_source	source_parallel[SUN6I_CSI_SOURCE_PARALLEL_MAX];
 	struct sun6i_csi_bridge_source	source_mipi_csi2;
+
+	/*
+	 * Whether the source was actually started, which is not the same as
+	 * whether it should have been: a pattern leaves it alone. The v4l2
+	 * core tracks each sub-device's streaming state and warns if it is
+	 * stopped without having been started, and the knob that decides this
+	 * can move while a stream is running, so remember what was done rather
+	 * than work it out again on the way down.
+	 */
+	bool				source_streaming;
 };
 
 /* Format */
